WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.540
The green cushion of moss on a shady wall is haploid.

2
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:12.660
Its cells carry one set of chromosomes, the same count as a human egg.

3
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:18.100
In your body, cells with one set exist only as eggs and sperm.

4
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:20.900
So where is the diploid moss?

5
00:00:21.783 --> 00:00:26.703
Land plants grow two multicellular bodies in one life cycle.

6
00:00:27.303 --> 00:00:32.323
The haploid body is the gametophyte, and the diploid body, with two sets of

7
00:00:32.323 --> 00:00:34.403
chromosomes, is the sporophyte.

8
00:00:35.063 --> 00:00:37.083
Each body gives rise to the other.

9
00:00:37.983 --> 00:00:40.843
Biologists call this alternation of generations.

10
00:00:41.683 --> 00:00:47.163
In humans and other mammals, meiosis makes eggs and sperm directly, and there is no

11
00:00:47.163 --> 00:00:48.163
haploid body.

12
00:00:48.817 --> 00:00:52.797
To read any life cycle, find two events first.

13
00:00:53.937 --> 00:00:58.057
Meiosis halves the chromosome number, from diploid to haploid.

14
00:00:58.937 --> 00:01:03.337
Fertilization joins egg and sperm, and restores the diploid number.

15
00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:09.457
Those are the only two places the number changes, so the stages between them share

16
00:01:09.457 --> 00:01:14.697
one label. Mitosis, which copies a cell, never changes it.

17
00:01:15.417 --> 00:01:21.897
In a land plant, cells of the sporophyte undergo meiosis, and the products are

18
00:01:21.897 --> 00:01:23.657
spores, not gametes.

19
00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:27.957
A spore divides by mitosis into the gametophyte.

20
00:01:28.617 --> 00:01:33.917
The gametophyte makes eggs and sperm by mitosis, because its cells are already

21
00:01:33.917 --> 00:01:39.297
haploid. Fertilization gives a zygote, the single fertilized cell.

22
00:01:39.297 --> 00:01:43.917
The zygote divides by mitosis into a new sporophyte.

23
00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:51.107
In a moss, the leafy green shoot is the gametophyte, and the sporophyte is a thin

24
00:01:51.107 --> 00:01:52.507
stalk with a capsule.

25
00:01:53.507 --> 00:01:59.607
In a fern, the frond is the sporophyte, and the gametophyte is a small prothallus

26
00:01:59.607 --> 00:02:00.747
that lives on its own.

27
00:02:01.627 --> 00:02:07.067
In a pine, the tree is the sporophyte, and the male gametophyte is a pollen grain.

28
00:02:08.007 --> 00:02:12.927
In the flowering plant Arabidopsis, the green plant is the sporophyte.

29
00:02:12.927 --> 00:02:16.547
The gametophytes are the pollen grain and the embryo sac.

30
00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.780
So the diploid moss was there all along.

31
00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.580
It is the stalk and capsule that grow from the zygote.

32
00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:31.460
The big body is the haploid gametophyte in a moss, but the diploid sporophyte in a

33
00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:33.740
fern, a pine and a flowering plant.

34
00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.200
So do not guess from size.

35
00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:41.600
Find meiosis and fertilization first, then label every stage.
